cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenTideConstants, cite the release you used by its release date
  and DOI, and also cite the upstream data sources of the stations you used
  (see https://opentideconstants.org/licence/).
  Release DOIs are coming with the first release.
title: "OpenTideConstants: open tidal harmonic constants"
abstract: >-
  An open dataset of tidal harmonic constants, rebuilt automatically from the
  latest upstream data, with declared conventions and published accuracy for
  every station.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "OpenTideConstants contributors"
url: "https://opentideconstants.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/opentideconstants/opentideconstants"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - tides
  - tidal harmonic constants
  - sea level
  - tide gauges
  - GESLA
# TODO with the first release: add version (YYYYMMDD), date-released, and
# identifiers (the Zenodo concept DOI and the version DOI).
